}}'''Olympus''' is a [[U.S. planetary commonwealth|US]] state located in the western edge of the Tharsis Plateau on [[Mars]]. The state is named after Olympus Mons, the tallest mountain and also one of the largest volcanoes in the [[Sol system|Solar System]]. The state is bordered by the Amazonian Sea to the west, [[Westylvania]] to the north, and the Tharsis Territory to the east and south.

== Geography and Climate ==
Western Olympus is largely characterized by the plainlands south of [[Wikipedia:Lycus Sulci|Lycus Sulci]]. The central part of the state is dominated by the Olympian Escarpment, and the eastern part of the state is a mountainous area home to Mount Olympus. The state has a subtropical climate, and two unnamed rivers also flow across the state. 
